#!/bin/sh
# script/initboot: boot nife-os with userspace init as the boot path (milestone 19d.2c).
# init brings up the console (and, in the interactive build, input and the shell) out of its own
# budget through the granular verbs; the kernel stops wiring services itself. Add --hvf for the
# real Apple Silicon core. See design/init-and-granular-spawn.md.
#
# Name: provisional, and this lane proposes a rename to `init-boot`. Introduced 2026-07-25 with
# milestone 19d.2c to boot with userspace init as the boot path. The name is not wrong about what
# it does; it is the **one entry point in this directory of fifty-two that runs two words
# together**, where every other multiword name is hyphenated and AGENTS.md's naming table makes
# that the rule, because a shell command is hyphenated everywhere outside this project and an
# underscore or a squish reads as a mistake. Milestone 63 made the rule and swept the tree on
# 2026-08-01 and this one survived the sweep rather than being exempted by it. The same holds one
# level along: `cargo xtask initboot` is likewise the only run-together subcommand beside
# `shell-check`, `board-console`, `initrd-aarch64` and `std-src`, so the rename is two strings
# rather than one. The Rust-side role it names is spelled `init_boot` in `user/src/hello.rs`,
# which is the same two words under the same table's other row. Proposed, not performed: a rename
# is calef's.
set -e
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
exec cargo xtask initboot "$@"
